x/sys v0.44.0 // indirect` already as a dependency\n   - The execution constitution forbids git commands, limits function size to 40 lines, requires SPDX headers\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd002-sys.yaml** (read)\n     - Contains the full SRD for pkg/sys with requirements R1 (Terminal width/TTY), R2 (Extended file metadata), R3 (SIGWINCH)\n     - R1.5 specifies: signal.Notify with buffered channel size 1, goroutine calling os.Exit(0), must not use signal.Ignore\n     - R1.6 specifies: safe to call multiple times\n     - R2.1 specifies: Stat/Lstat returning *FileInfo (already implemented)\n   \n   - **go.mod** (read)\n     - Module: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`, Go 1.26.3\n     - Has `require golang.org/x/sys v0.44.0 // indirect`\n     - Has `replace github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils => ./`\n   \n   - **pkg/sys/signal.go** (needs modification, current content from project_context):\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package sys\n     \n     // InstallSIGPIPEHandler installs a handler that exits the process with code 0\n     // when a SIGPIPE signal is received.\n     // R1.5: matches GNU coreutils behavior for piped output.\n     // R1.6: safe to call multiple times.\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n     }\n     \n     // OnTerminalResize registers a callback invoked with the new terminal width\n     // when a SIGWINCH signal is received.\n     // R3.1: calls TerminalWidth() and skips the callback if it returns an error.\n     // R3.2: supports multiple registered callbacks, called in registration order.\n     func OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int)) {\n     }\n     ```\n     - Needs: imports for os, os/signal, syscall; implementation body for InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n   \n   - **pkg/sys/terminal.go** (needs modification, current content from project_context):\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package sys\n     \n     // TerminalWidth returns the current terminal column count by querying stdout.\n     // R1.1: returns an error when stdout is not a terminal.\n     func TerminalWidth() (int, error) {\n     \treturn 0, nil\n     }\n     \n     // IsTerminal reports whether the file descriptor refers to a terminal.\n     // R1.3: returns false for pipes, regular files, and non-terminal descriptors.\n     func IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool {\n     \treturn false\n     }\n     ```\n     - Needs: imports for fmt, os, golang.org/x/sys/unix; real implementations using unix.IoctlGetWinsize\n   \n   - **pkg/sys/fileinfo.go** (in files list as modify but likely no changes needed - Stat/Lstat already implemented)\n   - **pkg/sys/stat_darwin.go** (already implemented, not in scope)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Write tool error on signal.go**: \"File has not been read yet. Read it first before writing to it.\" \n     - I attempted to Write signal.go without first Reading it with the Read tool. The Write tool requires a prior Read of the file.\n     - Fix needed: Must Read signal.go first, then Write or Edit it.\n     - Note: signal.go content IS available in the project_context source_code section, but the Write tool still requires an explicit Read call.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the task description has some labeling confusion: task R4 says \"R2.1 -- TerminalWidth\" but SRD R2.1 is actually about Stat/Lstat. The actual TerminalWidth requirement is SRD R1.1. However, the intent is clear from AC3.\n   - Determined that fileinfo.go likely doesn't need changes since Stat/Lstat (R2.1) are already implemented by a prior task.\n   - Determined signal.go must be modified even though it's not in the files list, because requirements R1.5/R1.6 explicitly demand implementing InstallSIGPIPEHandler which lives there.\n   - Confirmed golang.org/x/sys is already in go.mod as a dependency.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: The entire task description with role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source_code, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, constraints, shared_protocols, and package_contracts. This is the automated stitch task prompt.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Instructing to provide a summary without tool calls.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Read signal.go using Read tool (required before Write/Edit)\n   - Read terminal.go using Read tool (required before Write/Edit)\n   - Write/modify signal.go with InstallSIGPIPEHandler implementation\n   - Write/modify terminal.go with TerminalWidth and IsTerminal implementations\n   - Run `go build ./pkg/sys/...` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./pkg/sys/...` to verify (AC2)\n   - Verify AC3 and AC4\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was about to write the implementation for two files. The planned code changes are:\n\n   **signal.go** - new content:\n   ```go\n   // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n   // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n   \n   package sys\n   \n   import (\n   \t\"os\"\n   \t\"os/signal\"\n   \t\"syscall\"\n   )\n   \n   // InstallSIGPIPEHandler installs a handler that exits the process with code 0\n   // when a SIGPIPE signal is received.\n   // R1.5: matches GNU coreutils behavior for piped output.\n   // R1.6: safe to call multiple times.\n   func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n   \tc := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n   \tsignal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n   \tgo func() {\n   \t\t<-c\n   \t\tos.Exit(0)\n   \t}()\n   }\n   \n   // OnTerminalResize registers a callback invoked with the new terminal width\n   // when a SIGWINCH signal is received.\n   // R3.1: calls TerminalWidth() and skips the callback if it returns an error.\n   // R3.2: supports multiple registered callbacks, called in registration order.\n   func OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int)) {\n   }\n   ```\n\n   **terminal.go** - new content:\n   ```go\n   // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n   // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n   \n   package sys\n   \n   import (\n   \t\"fmt\"\n   \t\"os\"\n   \n   \t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n   )\n   \n   // TerminalWidth returns the current terminal column count by querying stdout.\n   // R1.1: returns an error when stdout is not a terminal.\n   func TerminalWidth() (int, error) {\n   \tws, err := unix.IoctlGetWinsize(int(os.Stdout.Fd()), unix.TIOCGWINSZ)\n   \tif err != nil {\n   \t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"sys: terminal width: %w\", err)\n   \t}\n   \treturn int(ws.Col), nil\n   }\n   \n   // IsTerminal reports whether the file descriptor refers to a terminal.\n   // R1.3: returns false for pipes, regular files, and non-terminal descriptors.\n   func IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool {\n   \t_, err := unix.IoctlGetWinsize(int(fd), unix.TIOCGWINSZ)\n   \treturn err == nil\n   }\n   ```\n\n   I attempted to Write signal.go but got an error because I hadn't Read the file first. The Write tool requires a prior Read call even though the file content is available in project_context.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Read signal.go and terminal.go using the Read tool, then Write both files with the implementations shown above, then run `go build ./pkg/sys/...` and `go vet ./pkg/sys/...` to verify compilation.\n   \n   The task I was working on: implementing srd002-sys R1.5 (InstallSIGPIPEHandler), R1.6 (safe to call multiple times), and TerminalWidth using TIOCGWINSZ ioctl. I had the code ready but hit the Write tool prerequisite error on signal.go.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5069/8ca0b4d7-76b3-4bb3-8424-94cca0819a0e.j